
That link is a GitHub Pages-style URL, and it is made of:

https:// = secure web URL
tulusma.github.io = your GitHub Pages domain
/tts = the repository name
/mandarin-lengkap 3.html = the HTML file inside the published site
So in plain structure:

https://{username}.github.io/{repo-name}/{file-name}

For your example:

username = tulusma
repo = tts
file = mandarin-lengkap 3.html
So it means:

“Open the file named mandarin-lengkap 3.html inside the tts project on GitHub Pages”
Important:

A space in a URL must be encoded as %20
So the valid URL should normally be:
https://tulusma.github.io/tts/mandarin-lengkap%203.html

The version you posted, with a plain space: https://tulusma.github.io/tts/mandarin-lengkap 3.html

may not work in many browsers because spaces are not valid unencoded in URLs.

If you want, I can also tell you whether this link points to:

a GitHub Pages site,
a raw HTML file,
or a repo file URL that should be converted to the correct browser link.
